## Canonical Entity Rules
- `character_a` / `character_b` can only use roster canonical names; the relationship matrix is not a registration entry for old names, aliases, organizations, or props.
- If old names, misnames, past-life names, or titles truly affect relationships, they can only appear as short evidence in `description`, not as relationship endpoints.
- `identity_link` only describes identity connections between two roster entities; aliases of the same entity should not be output as two separate character relationships.
- Downstream CharacterSystem will project this fragment into relationship edges; therefore each edge must be locally consumable by chapter prompts and cannot contain character bulk.

